# Miner Llama v5 preset (in progress): Flint, Flint Pascal Q8 GGUF (p065) on nine P106-090 cards, 262,144-token context.
# Build: the v5 engine, pascal-p106-v5 at 602691153 or later (upstream b12483 merged). Its P106 check gave this file the
# same greedy replies, memory on every card and kernel launches as v4.0 (docs/data/2026-11-18_c854b_p106_check/).
# v4.0's engine reads every switch below as well; the switch added here was measured on it.
# This is v4.0's preset (release/flint-v4/settings.env, explained in release/flint-v4/README.md) with one switch added,
# LLAMA_SERVER_TEXT_REUSE=1. On the coding-agent check on v4.0, two runs with it against the release check's two runs
# without it (docs/data/2026-11-17_r17_flint_textreuse/): no reply token read again, where the runs without it read
# 14,632 and 24,755 reply tokens again on 4 and 5 turns (67.6 of 222.6 s and 141.7 of 299.5 s of prompt time); prompt
# tokens read a task 2,970 and 2,942 against 4,076 and 5,093; the longest first-token wait 11.68 and 12.57 s against
# 24.70 and 93.88; a task 1.81 and 1.74 minutes at equal work against 1.72 and 1.81; 12/12 and 12/12 tasks with it,
# 11/12 and 12/12 without. A gain on the work it removes, negligible on every time measure; added on the owner's word
# on 2026-11-19, with the same switch in Flash-Next's v5 preset.
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
PRESET_MODEL=flint-pascal-Q8.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_KV_SEQ_RM_BOUND=1"  # removing a sequence's positions visits only the cells it can change, the same cells and head: each dropped pipelined guess no longer sweeps all 262,144 cells (C740, Q1309; R122: -0.33 ms a step on Flash-Next)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2"  # a step's yield to the server's reader thread wakes it only when a read waits, the same replies (C741, Q1310; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1"  # the card's sampling chain (-bs, top-k 20) runs one top-k over its output rows and reads the logits unpadded, the same tokens (C691, Q1223; R83; the graph fixed by C802, Q1406)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_GRAPHS_FORCE=1"  # prompt micro-batches captured as CUDA graphs without the two-call warm-up; the same replies, no loss at any depth (C702; R165a)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SCHED_PER_SIZE_RESERVE=2"  # after a re-plan of the shared scheduler, the plan for the largest batch over the whole memory again; Flint re-plans in agent use (323 reallocations in R159a) (C818, Q1447; R143)
# v5 (2026-11-19, docs/data/2026-11-17_r17_flint_textreuse/):
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_TEXT_REUSE=1"  # the server keeps its cached tokens where a reply sent back spells the same text in other tokens, so it never reads that reply again (Q260; R17a, R17b)
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

# v3.0's line; every flag is explained in release/flint-v3/README.md:
PRESET_ARGS="--alias flint -ngl 99 -fa on -c 262144 -np 1 -b 512 -ub 128 -ts 6,6,5,5,6,5,5,6,6 -bs --ctx-checkpoints 4 --cache-ram 0 --temp 1.0 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 --pipe-depth 4"
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ctx-checkpoints-vram 4"  # a slot's newest four checkpoints on the cards: a restore takes 2 ms instead of 292 ms, and the host keeps ~200 MiB more free; no loss at any depth (Q440, Q548; R165b)
PRESET_ARGS="$PRESET_ARGS --ubatch-taper short=600:64"  # a prompt call of at most 600 tokens in micro-batches of 64, which the nine cards work on as a pipeline; on Flint the same numbers to the digit (KLD 0, perplexity 0.000 %; FN96), no loss at any depth (Q771; R165b)
